    "Counterexample present_bold_empty: Java does not consider <b></b> or <i></i> atomless. CommandCreoleStyle.matchingSize rejects a zero-body closed match, then its EOL alternative paints the closing tag. Java paints </b>, </i>, and size26 </b> across three lines; Rust emits three base-size13 spaces. Java canvas173x169 versus Rust145x153. The empty-stripe projection is internally consistent but inherits an incorrect upstream zero-atom classification from handle_tag/walk_with.",
    "The new line_segments space is justified by StripeSimple.getAtoms only after equivalent command recognition. Empty size commands use a different matchingSize (digit count) and do produce the intended base-style space; treating every syntactically empty style span alike is not valid.",
